<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - PacifiCare downgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - PacifiCare downgraded.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Schroder Wertheim analyst William McKeever said he downgraded PacifiCare Health Systems Inc to &quot;perform in line&quot; from outperform.</p>
<p>-- cut his 1997 earnings per share estimate to $4.82 a share from $5.05, and cut 1998 estimate to $5.90 from $6.00.</p>
<p>-- cited weaker-than-expected enrollment growth. California Medicare markets are &quot;a bit saturated right now,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- expects it will take &quot;quite a while&quot; to improve profitability of operations at FHP International Corp, recently acquired by PacifiCare.  </p>
<p>-- PacifiCare is a &quot;show-me stock now,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- The stock was off 3-1/2 to 67-3/4.</p>
</text>
